.TH MPF-CLI 1 "2026-11-19" "MPF 3.11.1 (6daa0e50)" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mpf-cli \- dump a disc with redumper, aaru, DiscImageCreator or dreamdump and write its submission info
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mpf-cli
.I system
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B mpf-cli
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mpf-cli
(upstream \fBMPF.CLI\fR) is the command-line program of the Media
Preservation Frontend (MPF). It runs one of the dumping programs
on a drive and then, in the same process, reads the dump and its logs
and writes the Redump submission information (\fI!submissionInfo.txt\fR)
next to the output, the same step
.BR mpf-check (1)
performs on its own.
.PP
.I system
is a system code such as
.B pc
or
.BR psx ;
.B mpf-cli listsystems
prints them all. All other settings come from the configuration file
(see \fBCONFIGURATION\fR); the options below override them for one run.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR ? ", " h ", " help
Print the help text.
.TP
.B version
Print the program version.
.TP
.BR lc ", " listcodes
List the comment and content site codes.
.TP
.BR lo ", " listconfig
List the current configuration values.
.TP
.BR lpm ", " listpath
List the path macros (\fB%SYSTEM%\fR, \fB%DATE%\fR, ...).
.TP
.BR lm ", " listmedia
List the media type codes.
.TP
.BR ls ", " listsystems
List the system codes.
.TP
.BR lp ", " listprograms
List the dumping programs whose output MPF reads.
.TP
.BR i ", " interactive
Ask for every setting in a menu instead of taking options.
.TP
.B man
Print a manual page generated from the program's own option list.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-use " \fIprogram\fR"
Use this dumping program instead of the configured one:
.BR redumper ,
.BR aaru ,
.B dic
or
.BR dreamdump .
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-mediatype " \fImediatype\fR"
The media type (\fBmpf-cli listmedia\fR). Required for DiscImageCreator.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-device " \fIdevicepath\fR"
The drive, for example
.IR /dev/sr0 .
Required unless \fB\-c\fR is given.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mounted " \fIdirpath\fR"
Where the disc's filesystem is mounted, for the additional checks that
read files from it. Recommended on Linux, where the drive is a block device.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-file " \fIfilepath\fR"
The output file path. Without it MPF writes
.IR track_<date-time> / track_<date-time> .bin
in the configured output directory.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-speed " \fIspeed\fR"
Override the configured dumping speed.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-retries " \fIretries\fR"
Override the configured retry count.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-custom " \fIparams\fR"
Pass these parameters to the dumping program in place of the ones MPF
builds. They replace all of them, so they must be complete.
.SH CONFIGURATION
MPF reads
.I ~/.config/mpf/config.json
when it exists, and only otherwise a
.I config.json
next to the binary. The
.B mpf-cli
wrapper creates the file in your home before the first start, so that is
the one in use. It sets the four dumping-program paths to the names of the
packaged programs, which MPF finds on
.BR PATH :
.BR redumper-mpf ,
.BR aaru5 ,
.B DiscImageCreator.out
(package \fBdiscimagecreator\fR) and
.BR dreamdump .
.B mpf-cli
recommends these packages but does not require them; install the ones you
want to dump with.
The wrapper sets a path back to that name only when the configured one no
longer resolves (this needs
.BR jq ),
so a path of your own stays as long as it exists.
.PP
.B redumper-mpf
and
.B aaru5
are the builds this MPF build was made for. The rolling
.B redumper
and
.B aaru
packages may be newer, and MPF does not check the version of the program it
starts.
.SH OUTPUT PATH
Upstream MPF defaults
.B DefaultOutputPath
to the relative directory
.IR ISO ,
which a relative path resolves against the directory
.B mpf-cli
was started from. The wrapper sets it to
.I ~/ISO
instead, and resets it whenever it is empty or relative. Any absolute path
you set stays.
.SH DRIVE ACCESS
.B mpf-cli
runs unprivileged and carries no file capabilities: it sends no drive
commands itself. The dumping program does, and
.BR redumper-mpf ,
.B aaru5
and
.B DiscImageCreator.out
are installed with the
.B cap_sys_rawio
file capability, which the kernel grants from the executed file no matter
who starts it.
.B dreamdump
is installed without it.
Read access to
.I /dev/sr*
comes from the
.B uaccess
rule at a local desktop seat; for a headless or SSH session add yourself to the
.B cdrom
group:
.PP
.RS
.B sudo usermod \-aG cdrom $USER
.RE
.SH OLDER SYSTEMS
MPF reads and writes its log archives (\fI*_logs.zip\fR) through a library
that needs glibc 2.34 or newer. Below that (Enterprise Linux 8 has 2.28),
compressing the logs fails and leaves an empty archive, and extracting an
archive writes every file from it as 0 bytes. There the wrapper turns
.B CompressLogFiles
off in the configuration and refuses to start MPF on an output whose
\fI_logs.zip\fR lists files. Leave log compression off on such a system.
.SH EXAMPLES
Dump a PC disc with redumper:
.PP
.RS
.B mpf-cli pc \-u redumper \-d /dev/sr0 \-f ~/ISO/disc/disc.bin
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/mpf-cli
The wrapper described above; it starts the binary below.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/mpf-cli/MPF.CLI
The self-contained .NET binary.
.TP
.I ~/.config/mpf/config.json
The configuration, shared with
.BR mpf-check (1)
and
.BR mpf-gui (1).
.SH NOTES
This page is written by hand against MPF 3.11.1 commit 6daa0e50. MPF is
packaged as a rolling build, so the installed binary may be newer;
.B mpf-cli help
prints the options it takes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpf-check (1),
.BR mpf-gui (1),
.BR redumper (1),
.BR aaru5 (1),
.BR discimagecreator (1),
.BR dreamdump (1)
.PP
